<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Upload a paper | AK Explained</title>
<meta name="description" content="Owner-only page for adding a login-only question paper.">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">
<link rel="icon" href="/assets/logo.png" type="image/png">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Literata:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css">
</head>
<body data-admin="upload">
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<header class="site-header"></header>

<main id="main">

<section class="pagehead">
  <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">U</span>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Owner only</p>
    <h1>Upload a paper</h1>
    <p class="lede">Add a login-only question paper from its file. The questions go straight into the database, never into the website's files.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap authwrap">

  <nav id="adminNav" class="adminnav" aria-label="Admin tools" hidden></nav>

  <div id="upNotice" class="authnotice" role="status">Checking your account&hellip;</div>

  <div id="upBody" hidden>

    <div class="authcard">
      <h2>1. Choose the question file</h2>
      <div class="formerror" id="upFileError" role="alert" hidden></div>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Question file (.json)</span>
        <input id="upFiles" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" multiple>
        <span class="hint">One file for each level. A mock test has one file. An MCQ set with an easy and a medium level has two.</span>
      </label>
      <ul class="uprep" id="upReport"></ul>
    </div>

    <div class="authcard" id="upDetails" hidden>
      <h2>2. Where does it go?</h2>
      <p class="small">You choose where this paper belongs. The right id is built from your choice, so the paper always lands in the right place &mdash; even if the file was made with a wrong id.</p>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Exam / series</span>
        <select id="upDest">
          <option value="">Choose one&hellip;</option>
          {%- for d in paperDestinations %}
          <option value="{{ d.id }}" data-exam="{{ d.examId or '' }}" data-kind="{{ d.kind }}" data-prefix="{{ d.prefix or '' }}" data-needs-age="{{ 'yes' if d.needsAge else '' }}" data-needs-paper="{{ 'yes' if d.needsPaper else '' }}" data-title-word="{{ d.titleWord }}" data-auto="{{ 'yes' if d.autoPage else '' }}" data-self-serve="{{ 'yes' if d.selfServe else '' }}" data-min="{{ d.minNumber or '' }}" data-max="{{ d.maxNumber or '' }}" data-number-note="{{ d.numberNote or '' }}" data-page-base="{{ d.pageBase or '' }}" data-page-route="{{ d.pageRoute or '' }}" data-page-levels="{{ (d.pageLevels or []) | join(',') }}" data-registry-plan="{{ 'yes' if d.usesRegistryPlan else '' }}" data-ids="{{ d.idsJson }}" data-title-note="{{ d.titleNote or '' }}">{{ d.label }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="field" id="upAgeWrap" hidden>
        <span>Which age?</span>
        <select id="upAge">
          <option value="">Choose the age&hellip;</option>
          {#- Every age is listed here once, tagged with its series. assets/upload-paper.js keeps only the ages of the series chosen above (British, American or Indian English). #}
          {%- for d in paperDestinations %}{% if d.needsAge %}{% for a in d.ages %}
          <option value="{{ a.slug }}" data-dest="{{ d.id }}">{{ a.name }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="field" id="upPaperWrap" hidden>
        <span>Which paper?</span>
        <select id="upPaper">
          <option value="">Choose the paper&hellip;</option>
          {%- for d in paperDestinations %}{% if d.needsPaper %}{% for pp in d.papers %}
          <option value="{{ pp.id }}" data-title="{{ pp.title }}" data-path="{{ pp.path }}">{{ pp.title }}</option>
          {%- endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        </select>
        <span class="hint">Only papers that are already planned on the site are listed. The paper's id is made from your choice.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="field" id="upNumberWrap">
        <span>Test / set number</span>
        <input id="upNumber" type="number" min="1" step="1" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off">
        <span class="hint">For a mock test, its number (for example 5). For an MCQ day, the day number (for example 13). For an MCQ set, the set number for that age.</span>
      </label>
      <p class="small" id="upSlugPreview" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <label class="field" id="upLevelWrap" hidden>
        <span>Which level?</span>
        <select id="upLevel">
          <option value="medium" selected>Medium</option>
          <option value="easy">Easy</option>
          <option value="hard">Hard</option>
        </select>
        <span class="hint">This file does not say which level it is. Mock tests and the UP PGT MCQ days are saved as Medium.</span>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Title</span>
        <input id="upTitle" type="text" autocomplete="off">
        <span class="hint">The name shown for this paper. It is filled in for you from your choice; change it if you want.</span>
        <span class="hint" id="upTitleNote"></span>
      </label>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Status</span>
        <select id="upStatus">
          <option value="draft" selected>Draft &mdash; only you can see it</option>
          <option value="live">Live &mdash; students can open it (a paid paper needs the pass)</option>
        </select>
        <span class="hint">Leave it on Draft until the pages for it are ready. You can make it live later.</span>
      </label>
    </div>

    <div class="authcard" id="upGo" hidden>
      <h2>3. Upload</h2>
      <div class="formerror" id="upError" role="alert" hidden></div>
      <p class="small" id="upSummary"></p>
      <button class="btn" id="upButton" type="button">Upload this paper</button>
    </div>

    <div class="authcard" id="upDone" hidden>
      <h2 id="upDoneTitle">Done</h2>
      <p class="upverdict" id="upVerdict" role="status"></p>
      <ul class="uprep" id="upDoneReport"></ul>
      <div class="upcopy" id="upCopy" hidden>
        <p class="small"><strong>Something needs fixing.</strong> Press the button, then paste the text to Claude. It has everything needed to find the cause and fix it.</p>
        <textarea id="upCopyText" rows="9" readonly aria-label="Text to paste to Claude"></textarea>
        <button class="btn" id="upCopyBtn" type="button">Copy this for Claude</button>
        <span class="small" id="upCopyNote" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="small">Keep your own copy of the file. The database is the only copy now &mdash; the file is not saved anywhere on the website.</p>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>

</main>

<footer class="site-footer"></footer>

<script type="application/json" id="upPlan">{{ uploadPlan.json | safe }}</script>
<script src="/assets/admin.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/upload-paper.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
